	<h2>Software Development</h2>

<p>We design, build, and maintain free software. Our creations include Devuan.org, Dynebolic.org, FreeJ, Frei0r, Tomb, and Interfacer. These tools are used and redistributed by individuals and organizations across many fields. We work with a diversity of languages, methods, and disciplines, because that mix is what makes good code. Everything we release grants everyone the freedom to use, study, share, and enhance it.</p>

	<h2>Consulting, Trainging and Education</h2>

<p>We help organizations and individuals navigate technology on their own terms. That can mean advising on infrastructure, guiding a migration, or teaching a team the practices behind the tools. We do not sell lock-in: we share what we know so you can keep going without us. And we mean everyone! Our ambition is to explain this work clearly enough for a small child to follow, because understanding should never require permission.</p>

	<h2>Community and Research</h2>

<p>We run community infrastructure and take on research projects that explore how technology serves people, not the other way around. We recycle old technology rather than create needs for new ones. What you get from Dyne.org is something harder to name than a service: a community that answers, a legacy you can build on, and people who stay. 
<br>
Join us or donate to keep this work alive.</p>
